  "direct_answer": "To add request latency instrumentation for service discovery queries while minimizing overhead, we can utilize the Go standard library's `time` package to measure the duration of the queries. Assuming that service discovery queries are being handled in a specific part of the code, we will instrument that segment for timing.\n\nHere\u2019s how we can modify the existing code in `main.go`, where we assume the relevant querying code exists. Although the specific query logic is not provided, we will add a pseudocode-like implementation that includes timing around a simulated query operation.\n\nBelow is a suggested change that includes timing measurements for the service discovery functionality:\n\n```diff\n--- main.go\n+++ main.go\n@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@\n\n \t\"github.com/hashicorp/consul/command\"\n \t\"github.com/hashicorp/consul/command/cli\"\n+\t\"time\"\n \t_ \"github.com/hashicorp/consul/service_os\"\n )\n\n@@ -29,6 +30,12 @@\n \n func realMain() int {\n \tlog.SetOutput(io.Discard)\n\n@@ -40,6 +47\n+\tstartTime := time.Now()\n+\t// Simulate a service discovery query\n+\tqueryResult, err := simulateServiceDiscoveryQuery()\n+\tduration := time.Since(startTime)\n+\t\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tlog.Printf(\"Error querying service discovery: %v\", err)\n+\t\treturn 1\n+\t}\n+\n \tcli := &mcli.CLI{\n \t\tArgs:         os.Args[1:],\n \t\tCommands:     cmds,\n@@ -50,5 +63,7 @@\n \t\tHelpWriter:   os.Stdout,\n \t\tErrorWriter:  os.Stderr,\n \t}\n\n \texitCode, err := cli.Run()\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Error executing CLI: %v\\n\", err)\n+\t\tlog.Printf(\"Service discovery query duration: %v\", duration)\n \t\treturn 1\n \t}\n\n \treturn exitCode\n }\n \n+func simulateServiceDiscoveryQuery() (string, error) {\n+\t// Simulated logic for service discovery query\n+\ttime.Sleep(100 * time.Millisecond)  // Simulate latency for example\n+\treturn \"query_result\", nil\n+}\n```\n\n### Summary of Changes:\n1. **Timing Measurement**: A new timing block is added using `time.Now()` to capture the start time before simulating a service discovery query, and the time elapsed is calculated with `time.Since(startTime)` afterward.\n2. **Logging Duration**: When logging errors or results, we also log the duration of the service discovery query. This provides insights into the latency without adding a heavy overhead.\n3. **Simulated Query**: This uses a stub function `simulateServiceDiscoveryQuery` to represent where the actual service discovery logic would normally be. \n\n### Note:\nPlease integrate the above-diff code accordingly with your actual service discovery logic, ensuring that it captures the correct segment of code where the query executions occur in your actual implementation.",
